    "senderName": "NWS Reno NV",
    "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued October 22 at 1:47AM PDT until October 22 at 5:00PM PDT by NWS Reno NV",
    "description": "* CHANGES...None.\n\n* WHAT...Snow above 8000 feet. Additional snow accumulations of 2 to\n6 inches with 8 to 10 inches along the highest mountain peaks.\nRidge winds gusting as high as 40 mph at times.\n\n* WHERE...Mono County.\n\n* WHEN...Until 5 PM PDT this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Plan on slippery road conditions. The hazardous\nconditions will impact the Thursday morning and evening commutes.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Brief bursts of heavy snow and locally higher\nsnowfall totals will be possible with any thunderstorms that\ndevelop today.",
    "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. The latest road conditions\nfor the state you are calling from can be obtained by calling 5 1 1.",
